Perseverance just added 91 meters to its Mars record in one day, beating prior benchmarks. This is fascinating Frontiers, episode 222. Navigation cameras on Perseverance captured fresh wheel tracks across the rocky floor of Jezero Crater on Saul 2006. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration, or NASA, reported. The same drive measured 299.6 feet on the rover's odometer. Those cameras recorded the terrain ahead and behind. Feeding engineers' data on wheel

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.500
slippage and rock interactions.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.620
The frames show the wheels cutting paths through loose regolith and small rocks on a bolder

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.400
strewn surface.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.480
Mission planners will use the new images to chart the next series of traverses as the

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.820
vehicle keeps exploring the ancient river delta.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.160
The distance also helped the mission surpass its previous cumulative total, and the team

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.300
is reviewing the latest imagery to pick the next waypoints while the vehicle remains in

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:54.860
good health.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:01:00.060
Confirmed, exoplanet systems fall into two architectural families in a large survey

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.080
published in Nature.

00:01:02.054 --> 00:01:06.774
One group features tightly packed inner planets orbiting stars with higher metalicity and

00:01:06.774 --> 00:01:07.394
greater mass.

00:01:07.974 --> 00:01:12.154
The second group shows wider orbital spacing around lower mass host stars.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:17.774
Researchers compiled the sample from transit and radial velocity detections gathered by multiple

00:01:17.774 --> 00:01:19.594
ground and space-based telescopes.

00:01:20.374 --> 00:01:24.774
Disk mass and composition appear to set the final architecture according to the division

00:01:24.774 --> 00:01:30.194
in the data. The study did not require new observations, and instead re-analyzed existing

00:01:30.194 --> 00:01:35.414
catalogues to uncover the pattern. Stretch some of those orbital distances down to a map of

00:01:35.414 --> 00:01:40.094
Canada, and the outermost world would sit roughly as far from the innermost as Toronto sits

00:01:40.094 --> 00:01:46.334
from Vancouver. All of that span assembled inside one rotating disc of gas and dust around a newborn

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:52.854
star. Gravity pulled a collapsing cloud into a flattened sheet, a thin pancake of material in orbit.

00:01:52.854 --> 00:01:56.434
it, ride a parcel of that gas inward and the temperature climbs.

00:01:56.954 --> 00:02:01.234
Close to the star, the heat leaves only rock and metal able to condense out of the mix.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:03.854
Farther from the star, the ice is survived.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:08.694
Those ice is stick together and lock in the raw solids that later worlds will use.

00:02:09.294 --> 00:02:12.314
Researchers examine thousands of planets already on the books.

00:02:12.854 --> 00:02:14.114
One result stands out.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:19.234
The architectural boundary tracks the host star's mass and the amount of heavy elements it contains.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:23.834
That points to the disk's starting conditions, setting the layout before the first planets

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:24.914
even finish forming.

00:02:25.714 --> 00:02:29.034
Catalogues now let us map the outcome across hundreds of systems.

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:34.074
No one has identified the exact trigger that decides which layout a disk produces when

00:02:34.074 --> 00:02:36.194
the stars themselves look nearly identical.

00:02:36.814 --> 00:02:40.974
The lingering question is whether an early burst of turbulence or a slight difference in

00:02:40.974 --> 00:02:45.354
the disk's initial magnetic field strength, tips the outcome one way or the other.

00:02:45.354 --> 00:02:51.574
The hot Jupiter wasp 189B carries elemental abundances in its atmosphere that closely mirror

00:02:51.574 --> 00:02:53.234
those measured in its host star.

00:02:54.074 --> 00:02:58.334
Astronomers captured the planet's transmission spectrum as it passed in front of that star,

00:02:58.714 --> 00:03:00.954
according to a report from SSB crack.

00:03:01.574 --> 00:03:06.294
High-resolution spectroscopy isolated the planet's atmospheric signal from the star's light.

00:03:06.874 --> 00:03:10.994
The elemental mix in the atmosphere sits nearly identical to the mix measured in the

00:03:10.994 --> 00:03:11.654
star itself.

00:03:11.654 --> 00:03:16.474
That direct chemical link points to a shared material reservoir during formation.

00:03:16.994 --> 00:03:22.654
The same data set the abundance is side by side rather than treating the planet as a separate chemical system.

00:03:23.374 --> 00:03:29.134
Astronaut Christina Koch will begin serving as NASA's acting deputy chief engineer on November 1st.

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:35.454
She follows Catherine Van Hooser, who retires on October 21st after more than 35 years at the agency.

00:03:36.154 --> 00:03:41.194
Koch previously completed 328 consecutive days aboard the International Space Station.

00:03:41.194 --> 00:03:45.894
She also flew as a mission specialist on the Artemis II crewed flight around the moon.

00:03:46.474 --> 00:03:50.734
In the new post, she will oversee technical reviews and mission readiness across NASA

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:53.694
programs while moving to management astronaut status.

00:03:54.294 --> 00:03:58.934
NASA Administrator Jared Isaacman noted that Koch has experienced engineering challenges

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:02.174
from both the development side and during actual space flight.

00:04:02.774 --> 00:04:07.294
Van Hooser's career included leading propulsion engineering on the Space Shuttle main engine,

00:04:07.294 --> 00:04:12.074
and serving as the first chief engineer for the Space Launch System Liquid Engines element.

00:04:12.674 --> 00:04:17.634
Senator John Hoveon introduced Project Atlas during an event at the University of North Dakota.

00:04:18.294 --> 00:04:24.794
The flag reported that the initiative aims to strengthen the state's contributions to space research and national security programs.

00:04:25.374 --> 00:04:31.374
NASA Administrator Jared Isaacman and leaders from the Golden Dome Initiative attended to underscore federal interest.

00:04:31.374 --> 00:04:36.394
The project will support new research facilities and training programs that prepare students

00:04:36.394 --> 00:04:38.214
for roles in aerospace and defense.

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:43.274
The University of North Dakota will serve as the hub for partnerships that connect academic

00:04:43.274 --> 00:04:45.694
work with ongoing federal space priorities.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:51.514
Officials expect the effort to create pathways for North Dakota graduates into NASA and industry

00:04:51.514 --> 00:04:51.994
missions.

00:04:52.654 --> 00:04:57.414
Voyager technologies completed nearly three months of environmental testing on its Griffin-1

00:04:57.414 --> 00:05:02.734
lunar lander at NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory in late September. The test campaign

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:08.134
exposed the spacecraft to launch vibrations, thermal extremes, and simulated landing loads.

00:05:08.834 --> 00:05:13.014
Final verification confirmed that all systems can withstand the full sequence from

00:05:13.014 --> 00:05:18.614
liftoff through touchdown on the lunar surface. The lander carries Astrolab's flip rover and

00:05:18.614 --> 00:05:23.654
several additional payloads destined for the moon's south polar region. With testing complete,

00:05:23.654 --> 00:05:27.434
the spacecraft moves into final integration and launch preparations.

00:05:28.054 --> 00:05:32.894
The mission will demonstrate precision landing near Maun's Muton, close to the rim of

00:05:32.894 --> 00:05:33.774
Nobel Crater.

